00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:13,120
But as the king of the universe with all the wisdom that exists, inviting us to be a part of his one true kingdom.

202
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:16,460
Jesus' message is clear and compelling.

203
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:22,860
It is bold in delivery, and it has far-reaching implications for our lives.

204
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:28,180
Although it is clear on the surface, I think there's layers to this application.

205
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:38,860
I think if we're going to get the nuance of the application that Jesus is making, we've got to ask ourselves, what are the storms, and what or who is the house?

206
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:44,900
And it might seem like that's an easy enough question to answer, but I think it's a bit more nuanced than we might think.

207
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:51,320
So let's start with, what are the storms of our lives that Jesus is referring to?

208
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:59,860
I think there, based on my study, I think there's three different types of storms that Jesus might have in mind in his giving of this message.

209
00:18:59,860 --> 00:19:05,300
I have been doing, believe it or not, I feel far away from you all.

210
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:06,240
I'm feeling brave.

211
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:14,080
Believe it or not, I am trying hard to shorten my sermons.

212
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:17,240
And this week, I was like, you know what?

213
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:18,300
I have too much content.

214
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,080
So I did something.

215
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,960
We're going to cover two of the three storms.

216
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:24,600
And one of the storms, I recorded a short video.

217
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:25,720
We're going to put it in the newsletter.

218
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:28,660
So if you want bonus content, come back for more.

219
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:29,580
Join the newsletter.

220
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:30,860
This is dangerous.

221
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:37,200
But for now, we're just going to cover two of the three storms so that I finish on time.

222
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:37,700
Sound good?

223
00:19:37,700 --> 00:19:39,060
All right.

224
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:39,660
The first.

225
00:19:39,660 --> 00:19:41,080
Somebody's like, no, keep going.

226
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:45,140
I heard you guys after Corey's message last week.

227
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:45,900
I know you don't mean it.

228
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:57,620
The first type of storm that I think Jesus has in mind is individual storms.

229
00:19:57,620 --> 00:19:59,460
Individual storms.

230
00:19:59,460 --> 00:20:01,760
Storms that impact us personally.

231
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:06,860
And even in that type of storm, there's two versions of this type of storm.

232
00:20:06,860 --> 00:20:12,720
Proverbs chapter 26, verse 27 says, whoever digs a pit will fall into it.

233
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:16,320
If someone rolls a stone, it will roll back on them.

234
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:26,700
And what Solomon is saying here is if you do, if you make enough decisions where you're trying to take advantage of people by digging holes for them to fall into, eventually you will fall into your own hole.

235
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:39,020
And I think what Jesus is saying here is if we reject his teachings, if we reject his authority in our lives, we will end up making a pattern of destructive decisions that will lead to storms in our own life.

236
00:20:39,220 --> 00:20:46,700
We can create storms in our life by disobedience to the teachings of Jesus, by not submitting to the authority of Jesus.

237
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:52,340
We lie, we steal, we cheat, we gossip, we self-medicate, and we lust to get what we want in the moment.

238
00:20:52,340 --> 00:20:54,980
And it will eventually catch up to us.

239
00:20:54,980 --> 00:21:04,260
If you refuse to obey the teachings of Jesus, eventually you will bring about storms in your life from the decisions that you make.

240
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:09,580
Many of us in the room this morning know this all too well.

241
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:16,380
Many of us in here have experienced the crushing blow of storms in our life.

242
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:22,420
And we know when we lay our head down on the pillow at night, we know that those storms were caused by our own decisions.

243
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:29,800
The decisions that we made, the pattern of unchecked sin, of refusal to confess, of refusal to repent.

244
00:21:30,100 --> 00:21:31,860
We have created storms in our life.

245
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:38,380
Those storms have impacted those around us because of the decisions that we have made.

246
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:44,620
Not only are some of us in the room here and have already faced the storms of life that we caused by the decisions that we make,

247
00:21:44,620 --> 00:21:47,780
but I believe God sent me here this morning to tell some of you,

248
00:21:47,780 --> 00:21:53,460
you are on a pattern of decision-making that will create a storm,

249
00:21:53,460 --> 00:21:55,820
that will bring your house crashing down.

250
00:21:55,820 --> 00:22:03,560
Some of you have patterns of unchecked sin, things that you're hiding, things that you're not being honest about.

251
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:08,220
You're presenting yourself to your family, to your friends, and to your church as something that you are not.

252
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:13,540
And I believe God wants me to warn you that today, it's not too late.

253
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:19,700
You have an opportunity now to come clean, to confess, to be honest, to be open about the things that you've done,

254
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:24,000
and to receive God's healing and his mercy and his forgiveness.

255
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:31,120
And those of you that have created storms in your life because of decisions that you have made,

256
00:22:31,220 --> 00:22:35,840
you do not have to stay there in shame or regret or guilt.

257
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:38,220
You can pick yourself up.

258
00:22:38,220 --> 00:22:41,780
You can seek repentance and forgiveness from God.

259
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:47,240
You can do what you need to do to get yourself straight, to get out of the patterns and decisions that you've made.

260
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:52,460
You can go to the people that you have hurt, and you can seek forgiveness and reconciliation.

261
00:22:53,960 --> 00:23:00,380
And whether or not they receive that repentance, whether or not they extend you forgiveness,

262
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:02,760
just know that God and Christ has forgiven you.

263
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:05,420
And you can't control their response.

264
00:23:05,420 --> 00:23:08,320
All you can control is what you do with the decisions that you've made.

265
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:16,160
We can avoid some storms in our life if we get serious about obeying the teachings of Jesus.

266
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:21,260
The good news is that there is healing, forgiveness, and restoration through Jesus.

267
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:23,140
Don't stay in the pit.

268
00:23:23,140 --> 00:23:24,880
Receive his grace and his forgiveness.

269
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:28,740
The second version of individual storms, you might have guessed,

270
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:32,180
are storms that happen to you because of decisions that others have made.

271
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:38,760
This is the most devastating type of storm because often you had no control over it whatsoever.

272
00:23:38,760 --> 00:23:45,340
A loved one, a father, a mother, a husband, a wife, a friend betrayed you, lied to you.

273
00:23:45,340 --> 00:23:47,200
They presented to you something that wasn't true.

274
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:50,380
And eventually the truth came out.

275
00:23:51,720 --> 00:23:58,220
We cannot avoid these storms, but we can lessen their impact by building our life on the rock,

276
00:23:58,220 --> 00:24:00,340
by having eternal perspective.

277
00:24:00,340 --> 00:24:02,200
The decisions of others, listen to me.

278
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:05,920
For those of you that have experienced pain, for those of you that have been abused,

279
00:24:05,920 --> 00:24:09,520
for those of you that have been taken advantage of by those who are supposed to keep you safe,

280
00:24:09,520 --> 00:24:14,060
for those of you that have had storms come to your life because of decisions that others have made on you,

281
00:24:14,060 --> 00:24:14,480
hear this.

282
00:24:14,560 --> 00:24:17,420
The decisions of others do not have to define you.

283
00:24:17,420 --> 00:24:22,760
Your identity is not found in the decision of others, but in what God says about you.

284
00:24:24,340 --> 00:24:33,300
Extend forgiveness, turn the other cheek, trust in God who is the eternal and just judge who will wipe away every tear from our eyes.

285
00:24:35,020 --> 00:24:42,200
If someone, if you're experiencing storms that have been caused by others, don't allow them to have that much power over your life.

286
00:24:42,300 --> 00:24:48,020
Go to the Lord and receive his healing and redemptive power.

287
00:24:48,020 --> 00:24:50,200
There's individual storms.

288
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:53,560
There's corporate storms that we don't have time to go over.

289
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:55,500
So subscribe to the newsletter.

290
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:01,400
It's almost like I went to, they should call Bible college marketing school.

291
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:05,220
Just like a cheap version, bad marketing school.

292
00:25:05,220 --> 00:25:05,520
Okay.

293
00:25:05,520 --> 00:25:12,020
Last type of storm is the cosmic storm, the ultimate storm that is coming for all of us, no matter how we live.

294
00:25:12,020 --> 00:25:16,300
Death and the grave is on the horizon of all of us.

295
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:21,800
Death has a 100% satisfaction guarantee rate, right?

296
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:23,380
There's no avoiding it.

297
00:25:24,220 --> 00:25:28,200
And yet Jesus seems to say that there's a way that we can live.

298
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:35,180
There's a way we can build our lives that will allow us to persevere even death and the grave itself.

299
00:25:35,180 --> 00:25:38,420
Which leads us to our last question.

300
00:25:38,420 --> 00:25:40,720
Who or what is the rock?

301
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:48,080
Anybody who was a A plus Sunday school student want to yell out what they think the answer to this question might be?

302
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:50,980
Yeah, there we go.

303
00:25:50,980 --> 00:25:53,260
Jesus is the rock.

304
00:25:53,800 --> 00:25:59,960
In the Old Testament, the rock is thought of as the temple of Jerusalem sitting on top of the rock.

305
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:07,720
All who would build their lives in genuine obedience to and worship to the one true God would persevere.

306
00:26:07,720 --> 00:26:08,820
Wow, that one's a hard one.

307
00:26:08,820 --> 00:26:11,460
Any storm they might face.

308
00:26:12,440 --> 00:26:21,800
But now as we turn our eyes to Jesus in the New Testament, he will go on to say, tear the temple down and I will rebuild it in three days.

309
00:26:23,320 --> 00:26:27,680
Obviously, in hindsight, that's referring to his death and resurrection.

310
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:40,820
The life, the victory and the teachings of Jesus become the one true rock that if we build our lives on, faith in him and obedience to his teachings, we will be able to weather any storm.

311
00:26:41,480 --> 00:26:42,720
Even the storm of death itself.

312
00:26:42,720 --> 00:26:44,180
Even the storm of death itself.

313
00:26:44,180 --> 00:26:47,820
And his resurrection proves this.

314
00:26:47,820 --> 00:26:52,660
I said it was a 100% satisfaction guarantee except for one time in human history.

315
00:26:52,660 --> 00:26:56,700
And that is the reason that you and I are here because Jesus did die.

316
00:26:56,700 --> 00:27:00,940
He was buried and he did raise from the dead.

317
00:27:00,940 --> 00:27:02,620
And if he didn't, we're wasting our time.

318
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:14,320
But if he did, building our house on faith in him and obedience to his teachings will allow us to persevere even the cosmic storm of death itself.

319
00:27:14,320 --> 00:27:15,640
Tim Mackey says it this way.

320
00:27:15,640 --> 00:27:20,480
Jesus becomes the first one whose house on a rock withstands the flood.

321
00:27:20,480 --> 00:27:24,880
He goes through the storm for us.

322
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:30,100
He weathers the storm of decisions of others.

323
00:27:30,100 --> 00:27:32,060
Think about it.

324
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:39,520
Jesus, as he's going to the cross, he's weathering the storm of the decision of Judas to betray him.

325
00:27:39,520 --> 00:27:45,260
Of the decision of Pilate to not stand up for what's right, but to just give the people what they want.

326
00:27:45,260 --> 00:27:50,300
Of the decisions of the nation of Israel who have rejected their Messiah and said, give us Barabbas.

327
00:27:50,300 --> 00:27:54,160
Jesus is weathering the storms of decisions that other people have made.

328
00:27:54,160 --> 00:27:59,100
He is setting an example for us, trusting himself to the Lord who judges justly.

329
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:03,360
And he goes to the cross and the very people that are mocking him and spitting him in his face.

330
00:28:03,360 --> 00:28:06,580
He says, Father, forgive them for they do not know what they are doing.

331
00:28:06,580 --> 00:28:09,720
He dies and they think they've had victory.

332
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:12,980
They think some lunatic or liar has died.

333
00:28:12,980 --> 00:28:14,400
And finally, we're done with him.

334
00:28:14,500 --> 00:28:20,160
But three days later, he raises from the grave, proving that he has had victory over sin, death, and the grave.

335
00:28:20,160 --> 00:28:25,560
He becomes the first one whose house on a rock withstands the flood of death itself.

336
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:43,860
And if we want to persevere the storms of death and the storms of death, we do so not by just thinking positive thoughts about Jesus's life, but by faith in and obedience to his teachings.

337
00:28:43,860 --> 00:28:47,740
All right.

338
00:28:47,740 --> 00:28:59,140
So, as we wrap up, the question that I was thinking for myself this week, and band, you all can come up and prepare to kind of lead us in this concluding part.

339
00:28:59,140 --> 00:29:08,700
I was thinking to myself, I'm preaching a message on the application, the conclusion, the application of one of the best sermons Jesus has ever preached.

340
00:29:09,520 --> 00:29:16,280
How can I write an application about the application of one of Jesus's best sermons he's ever preached?

341
00:29:16,280 --> 00:29:25,740
I decided that the only move here is to steal a play out of Jesus's playbook and just ask you all a bunch of questions.

342
00:29:25,740 --> 00:29:27,600
I love that.

343
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:33,320
I love when Jesus, somebody asks Jesus a question and then he answers with a question.

344
00:29:33,320 --> 00:29:37,000
So, you might be thinking, what do I do with this message?

345
00:29:37,360 --> 00:29:39,700
Well, let me respond to you with some questions.

346
00:29:39,700 --> 00:29:49,320
First, is your discipleship to Jesus more focused on learning information or applying information?

347
00:29:49,320 --> 00:29:59,420
When you interact with the Scriptures, when you interact with other people about the Bible and Jesus, when you come to church or go to a passages class or join a small group,

348
00:29:59,420 --> 00:30:05,540
are you focused more on learning more information or doing what Jesus invites you to do?

349
00:30:05,540 --> 00:30:12,800
Do you believe that Jesus has the authority to command the direction of your entire life?

350
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:21,500
And if you would answer yes to that question, do your daily decisions reflect the answer to that question?

351
00:30:21,500 --> 00:30:31,640
Or are there certain areas in our life that we're like, yeah, he has the authority over most of my life, but not this part, not right now.

352
00:30:31,640 --> 00:30:38,140
Maybe later, once I get all the things I want out of this relationship or this pattern of sin,

353
00:30:38,560 --> 00:30:41,480
maybe one day I will hand it over to the Lord.

354
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:48,800
Have decisions you've made contributed to the storms of your life?

355
00:30:50,580 --> 00:30:58,440
Are there storms that you're facing and that others in your orbit are facing because of decisions that you made, patterns of sin that you participated in?

356
00:30:58,440 --> 00:31:02,160
A lack of repentance, a lack of confession.

357
00:31:02,160 --> 00:31:08,040
Did you allow yourself to get so far down a path that you fell into a hole and brought other people with you?

358
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:13,960
If that's you, what can you do to make an effort to calm those storms?

359
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:46,200
If you're in here and the storms of your life have been created by others and the decisions that others have made,

360
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:51,220
I'd ask you this question, are you allowing the decisions of others to have too much power over your life?

361
00:31:51,220 --> 00:31:59,780
What can you do to release some of the weight of the decisions that others have made and give them to God,

362
00:31:59,780 --> 00:32:01,880
building your house on his rock?

363
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:22,900
Are you building your life around faith in and obedience to Jesus in a way that will allow you to persevere inevitable storms of life and death?

364
00:32:26,700 --> 00:32:34,760
Today, I wanted to provide an opportunity to encourage those of us who are in the building, who we're building, we know, we know.

365
00:32:34,760 --> 00:32:37,940
We're not perfect, but we're building our life on the rock.

366
00:32:37,940 --> 00:32:38,880
I want to encourage you.

367
00:32:38,880 --> 00:32:40,660
If you're in here and you're like, yes, that's me.

368
00:32:40,660 --> 00:32:42,100
I am building my life on the rock.

369
00:32:42,100 --> 00:32:42,740
I'm not perfect.

370
00:32:42,740 --> 00:32:47,100
I'm not doing everything great, but I'm trying by faith and trust in the Holy Spirit.

371
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,920
I just want to encourage you today.

372
00:32:48,920 --> 00:32:49,880
I know it's hard.

373
00:32:49,880 --> 00:32:55,520
I know it'd be a lot easier to build your life on sand, but it's worth it.

374
00:32:55,520 --> 00:33:06,000
Your life will persevere any storm that you face if you continue to submit your life to faith in and obedience to Jesus.

375
00:33:10,840 --> 00:33:11,700
Be encouraged.

376
00:33:11,700 --> 00:33:15,040
The storms will come, but your life will persevere.

377
00:33:15,040 --> 00:33:23,860
The second group are those of you that know in the past you've made a decision to build your life on the rock.

378
00:33:23,860 --> 00:33:27,000
Maybe you went into the waters of baptism.

379
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:30,280
You've made that decision and you were following for a while.

380
00:33:30,280 --> 00:33:38,500
But at this moment in time, you look back at your life and you say, there's a trajectory of my life that's been leading me away.

381
00:33:40,180 --> 00:33:44,600
I started on the rock and now I'm building on top of that rock with sand.

382
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:51,400
I just wanted to provide an opportunity for people to just set up a monument.

383
00:33:51,400 --> 00:33:57,020
I got a bucket full of rocks up here and some Sharpies.

384
00:33:57,020 --> 00:34:00,800
I just want those of us that are thinking, yeah, that's me.

